# Testing

## Rules

- Framework: **Jest** for both unit tests and e2e tests.
- **No minimum coverage is enforced.**
- **Never create tests automatically or proactively.** Only write tests when the user explicitly requests them, specifying which use case or endpoint to test.

## Unit test structure (canonical)

All unit specs follow the same shape as `src/main.spec.ts`:

1. **Mocks first** — `jest.mock(...)` / Nest `useValue` mocks at the top (before `describe`).
2. **`describe('<unit>')`** — name matches the file/unit under test (`main`, `CreatePostUseCase`, …).
3. **Typed deps** — declare `let` mocks/subjects at the top of `describe`.
4. **`beforeEach`** — rebuild fresh mocks and wire return values every test.
5. **One behavior per `it`** — short `should …` title; a one-line comment above describing the expectation.
6. **Act → assert** — call the unit, then `expect(...).toHaveBeenCalledWith(...)` / value checks. No shared state across tests.

```typescript
// <unit>.spec.ts
jest.mock('some-external', () => ({
  SomeClient: { call: jest.fn() },
}));

describe('main', () => {
  let mockApp: { listen: jest.Mock };

  beforeEach(() => {
    mockApp = { listen: jest.fn() };
    (NestFactory.create as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue(mockApp);
  });

  // App should listen on defined port
  it('should listen on defined port', async () => {
    await bootstrap();

    expect(mockApp.listen).toHaveBeenCalledWith(process.env.PORT ?? 3000);
  });
});
```

### Use cases (Nest DI)

Same structure; mock the repository via its injection token with `useValue`:

```typescript
// application/use-cases/create-post/create-post.use-case.spec.ts
describe('CreatePostUseCase', () => {
  let useCase: CreatePostUseCase;
  let postRepository: jest.Mocked<IPostRepository>;

  beforeEach(async () => {
    const module = await Test.createTestingModule({
      providers: [
        CreatePostUseCase,
        {
          provide: POST_REPOSITORY,
          useValue: {
            save: jest.fn(),
            findBySlug: jest.fn(),
          } satisfies Partial<IPostRepository>,
        },
      ],
    }).compile();

    useCase = module.get(CreatePostUseCase);
    postRepository = module.get(POST_REPOSITORY);
  });

  // Post should be created and returned
  it('should create and return a post', async () => {
    const post = Post.create({ title: 'Hello', content: 'World', slug: 'hello' });
    postRepository.save.mockResolvedValue(post);

    const result = await useCase.execute({ title: 'Hello', content: 'World' });

    expect(postRepository.save).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);
    expect(result.title).toBe('Hello');
  });
});
```

## e2e tests (canonical)

Location: `test/<feature>.e2e-spec.ts`. Use `supertest` against the full NestJS app and a **dedicated test database** — never production or development data.

Same discipline as unit tests: one behavior per `it`, a one-line comment above each case.

### Lifecycle

1. Usa **`beforeAll`** para bootstrapping global de la app — solo una vez por suite e2e, nunca con `beforeEach`. Esto asegura performance y consistencia en los tests integrales. Replica los globals de `main.ts` para que la superficie HTTP coincida con producción: `setGlobalPrefix('api')`, `ValidationPipe` (`whitelist`, `forbidNonWhitelisted`, `transform`), y registra filtros globales como `AllExceptionsFilter`. Usa `cookieParser` en el flujo solo cuando los tests lo requieren (autenticación, sesiones, etc).
2. Usa **`beforeEach`** solo para restaurar/limpiar estado entre casos, si es necesario (por ejemplo, limpiar mocks, reiniciar datos específicos, o reinicializar fixtures pequeños). Nunca para reiniciar toda la app.
2. **Fixtures** — resolve the TypeORM entity with `getRepositoryToken(SomeTypeOrmEntity)` (never the domain entity). Delete existing rows by unique key, then insert the test records. Prefer the public HTTP create endpoint when it exists; otherwise `repository.insert` / `save`. This keeps re-runs idempotent if a previous suite left data behind.
3. **`afterAll`** — delete the same fixtures, then `await app.close()` to close the DB connection.

### `it` structure (mandatory)

Every case is `async`. Capture the HTTP call in `const response`, then assert on `response.status` and `response.body`. Never chain `.expect()` as the assertion style and never inspect the request without assigning `response`.

```typescript
const response = await request(app.getHttpServer())
  .post('/api/auth/login')
  .send(credentials);

expect(response.status).toBe(401);
expect(response.body.message).toEqual('…');
```

For class-validator 400s, collect the expected messages and `forEach` with `toContain`. For success bodies, compare with `toEqual` and `expect.any(Type)` for generated fields.

```typescript
// test/auth-login.e2e-spec.ts
import { Test, TestingModule } from '@nestjs/testing';
import { INestApplication, ValidationPipe } from '@nestjs/common';
import { AppModule } from '../src/app.module';
import { Repository } from 'typeorm';
import { getRepositoryToken } from '@nestjs/typeorm';
import request from 'supertest';
import cookieParser from 'cookie-parser';
import { AllExceptionsFilter } from '../src/common/filters/all-exceptions.filter';
import { AdminTypeOrmEntity } from '../src/modules/admin/infrastructure/persistence/typeorm/admin.typeorm-entity';

const testingAdmin = {
  username: 'test.admin',
  password: 'Abc123',
  email: 'test.admin@email.com',
  name: 'Test',
  lastName: 'Admin',
};

describe('Auth login (e2e)', () => {
  let app: INestApplication;
  let adminRepository: Repository<AdminTypeOrmEntity>;

  beforeAll(async () => {
    const moduleFixture: TestingModule = await Test.createTestingModule({
      imports: [AppModule],
    }).compile();

    app = moduleFixture.createNestApplication();
    app.setGlobalPrefix('api');
    app.use(cookieParser());
    app.useGlobalPipes(
      new ValidationPipe({
        whitelist: true,
        forbidNonWhitelisted: true,
        transform: true,
        transformOptions: { enableImplicitConversion: true },
      }),
    );
    app.useGlobalFilters(new AllExceptionsFilter());
    await app.init();

    adminRepository = app.get<Repository<AdminTypeOrmEntity>>(
      getRepositoryToken(AdminTypeOrmEntity),
    );

    await adminRepository.delete({ username: testingAdmin.username });
    // Seed via HTTP when a create endpoint exists; otherwise repository insert/save.
    await request(app.getHttpServer()).post('/api/admins').send(testingAdmin);
  });

  afterAll(async () => {
    await adminRepository.delete({ username: testingAdmin.username });
    await app.close();
  });

  // Login without a body should return 400
  it('POST /api/auth/login should throw if no body', async () => {
    const response = await request(app.getHttpServer()).post('/api/auth/login');

    const errorMessages = [
      'username must be a string',
      'password must be a string',
    ];

    expect(response.status).toBe(400);
    errorMessages.forEach((message) => {
      expect(response.body.message).toContain(message);
    });
  });

  // Login with a wrong username should return 401
  it('POST /api/auth/login should throw if wrong username', async () => {
    const credentials = { username: 'missing.admin', password: 'Password1' };

    const response = await request(app.getHttpServer())
      .post('/api/auth/login')
      .send(credentials);

    expect(response.status).toBe(401);
    expect(response.body.message).toEqual('Usuario o contraseña incorrectos');
  });

  // Successful login should return the wrapped payload
  it('POST /api/auth/login should login successfully', async () => {
    const credentials = {
      username: testingAdmin.username,
      password: testingAdmin.password,
    };

    const response = await request(app.getHttpServer())
      .post('/api/auth/login')
      .send(credentials);

    expect(response.status).toBe(201);
    expect(response.body).toEqual({
      status: 'ok',
      message: expect.any(String),
      data: {
        accessToken: expect.any(String),
        admin: {
          id: expect.any(String),
          username: credentials.username,
          name: testingAdmin.name,
          lastName: testingAdmin.lastName,
        },
      },
    });
  });
});
```

## npm scripts (reference)

```json
"scripts": {
  "test":     "jest",
  "test:e2e": "jest --config ./test/jest-e2e.json"
}
```
